# E05 short break (RE-2): live DLL recovery capture, 2026-11-04, Finam demo server.
# Logging proxy -> demo; the proxy was killed for ~5 s and restarted, the DLL
# recovered by itself: no new RQ_LOGIN/RQ_PWD/RQ_STARTUP on the second connection.
#
# Format: <direction> <request type> <payload hex>  (decrypted payload bytes).
# Login is anonymized to TESTLOGIN per the RE-2 rules. The captured RQ_RELOGIN
# carried the Z12 login of another (8-byte) string; the anonymized Z12 is one byte
# longer because Z12 is a NUL-terminated variable-length field. Everything else is
# byte-exact. Token and lastSeq are server session data, not account data.
# Raw captures stay outside git: .re-run/cap/recover-short-{a,b}.cap.
#
# RQ_RELOGIN(63) is sent on the default keys; RQ_RECOVER(64) on the session keys.
# RQ_RELOGIN reply: B:len=135, Bn:token len=135, B:sid=0.
# RQ_RECOVER payload: token(no length prefix) + packed L:lastSeq=61.

C>S 63 544553544c4f47494e00
S>C 63 87ef5e1d2062f81d540f2175d8b28095d6aa8743ab7ddc7a3f192b3bf3e229696247330c6dbdc0b831d9689b4d9eaecb1ae16a87432aac1585fab1c42e8115787865fb588ca626419d2d3cc18aadc65ca9208d68db6a74bc577bc88b12c3e851a1bcafde491a168321d916729bf7bc4e23a69d1241e7ad7ee7d2eba40f31b603925d28a5dae2293400
C>S 64 ef5e1d2062f81d540f2175d8b28095d6aa8743ab7ddc7a3f192b3bf3e229696247330c6dbdc0b831d9689b4d9eaecb1ae16a87432aac1585fab1c42e8115787865fb588ca626419d2d3cc18aadc65ca9208d68db6a74bc577bc88b12c3e851a1bcafde491a168321d916729bf7bc4e23a69d1241e7ad7ee7d2eba40f31b603925d28a5dae22934d103

# First frame after RQ_RECOVER: the server answers with the type of the interrupted
# request (RQ_MAIN, type 5) and 2216 payload bytes - the pending reply. The DLL accepts
# that type as the recover reply (RE-1: type 0x40 or the last ordinary request type).
S>C 5 

# Next RQ_MAIN poll after the recovery (empty payload).
C>S 5

